            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for unlikely, then the Persian for definite."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: قطعا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قطعا (qat'an) — \"definitely, certainly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او قطعا فردا میآید. u qat'an fardâ miâyad. He is definitely coming tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Close to hatman in meaning, and a little more formal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قطعا (qat'an) is usually traced to Arabic qaṭ'an \"decisively\", an adverb built on qaṭ' \"cutting\", like qat'i \"definite\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
