          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اطمینان (etminân) — \"certainty, confidence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "با اطمینان میگویم که حق با توست. bâ etminân miguyam ke haq bâ tost. I can say for certain that you are right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Etminân dâshtan — to be sure; etminân dâdan — to reassure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اطمینان (etminân) was borrowed from Arabic iṭmi'nān \"calm, assurance\" (EtymDB), from the same Arabic family as muṭma'inn \"sure\", the source of Persian motma'en."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
